        "Key line: philosophers \"annex every century\" to their own. Reading can extend life because it gives you access to minds outside your immediate time and social circle.",
        "Names/context: Socrates stands for questioning, Carneades for skeptical argument, Epicurus for peace, Stoics for self-command, Cynics for radical simplicity, Zeno for Stoic founding, Pythagoras and Democritus for older philosophical/scientific imagination, Aristotle and Theophrastus for systematic inquiry. Seneca is naming a library of possible companions.",
